 races run on national dynamics"], "rationale": "Rhode Island's eight-point Democratic lean is the clearest available signal, and with no polls, ratings, or market prices to weigh, the forecast stays at fundamentals while carrying wide uncertainty; local Democratic turbulence in the governor's race does not clearly transfer to a nationalized presidential contest.", "watch": "The first general-election polls of Rhode Island, or a decisive shift in the national political environment, would quickly move this forecast.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island enters the 2028 presidential race as a modest Democratic-leaning state, with a partisan lean of eight points toward Democrats and no incumbent on the ballot after the term-limited president leaves office. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or prediction-market prices are available yet, so the picture rests almost entirely on fundamentals.\n\nRhode Island has reliably backed Democrats in recent presidential elections, though state politics showed cracks in 2026 when the Democratic governor lost a primary amid anger over a bridge collapse. Presidential contests tend to turn on national dynamics rather than state issues, and the state's structural lean remains solidly Democratic. The forecast treats Rhode Island as Lean Democratic, with wide uncertainty given the absence of polling and ratings this early.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8249, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7734, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7988, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7688, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8114, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8082, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "20